NEARS-1837 QA — PRE-EXISTING a11y defect (NOT caused by this ticket; this ticket changes no
product code). Observed live on emulator-5554, BASELINE build md5 4cbaef2e42d553c1711be0b1a56b59d8.

WHERE: UserApp/lib/features/auth/widgets/select_location_view_widget.dart, the `widget.fromView`
fullscreen-expand control (30x30 Container, Icon(Icons.fullscreen_rounded, size 20)) inside the
Location Info card of Vendor Registration.

WHAT: the control has NO Semantics wrapper and no tooltip, so it projects NO accessibility
label. A screen-reader user cannot identify or reach it by name, and it is the ONLY route to
the fullscreen map (which is where the zoom controls live at all — the zoom card is gated on
`!widget.fromView`). Adjacent controls in the same widget DO carry labels
("Use my current location"), so this is an omission, not a platform limit.

RAW NODE (dump zoneset-d2.xml, emulator-5554, 2026-08-11):
  <node index="..." text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="com.izzes.nears"
   content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="true" enabled="true"
   focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false"
   password="false" selected="false" bounds="[1131,2221][1266,2311]" drawing-order="0" hint="" />

Same-dump positive control proving the dump is interpretable (i.e. the empty content-desc is a
real absence, not a dead instrument):
  <node ... class="android.widget.Button" content-desc="Use my current location" clickable="true"
   bounds="[1131,2341][1266,2431]" />

Bounds 135x90 px @ 480dpi = 45x30 dp — also under the 44dp minimum on one axis.

IMPACT: blocks a11y access to the whole fullscreen store-location map for TalkBack users.
QA had to resolve this node by a structural predicate because no label exists.
